CyberCipher crate `cybercipher-sstv` — provenance notice
=========================================================

This crate is a migration of the MIT-licensed `sstv-auto` project:

  repository: https://github.com/jacek4yang/sstv-auto
  commit:     f626d505e2928efaa7c217e21fb61fcf43686768
  license:    MIT (full text below)

What changed relative to upstream:
  * The library modules (audio, dsp, modes, vis, sync, raster, synth,
    autodetect, backend, score, pipeline, report) were migrated in-tree into
    the CyberCipher workspace with their algorithm code preserved verbatim
    where practical.
  * `anyhow` was replaced by a crate-local `SstvError` with drop-in
    `anyhow!`/`bail!`/`Context` equivalents (see src/error.rs) so module code
    and its tests keep their upstream shape.
  * The audio ingestion boundary gained a bytes-based entry point
    (`audio::load_bytes`, `pipeline::decode_bytes`) alongside the original
    path-based API; bytes-based runs never touch the filesystem and return
    decoded images in memory for explicit PNG serialization
    (`backend::encode_png`).
  * The upstream CLI binary (`main.rs`) is intentionally not migrated;
    CyberCipher exposes the pipeline through its operation registry and GUI.

The original MIT license text of sstv-auto follows.

